            <div xml:id="d378">

                <pb facs="0374" n="304" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg304"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">725.34/18: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sevier</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-07T20:00:00-04:00">August 7, 1934—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>66. Embassy’s telegram 65, August 6, 6 p.m. Foreign Office informs me that
                    presentation of its note to Paraguay has been delayed due to the telegraphic
                    garbles but that it will be delivered tonight and that Chilean Minister at
                    Asunción will depart next Sunday. Foreign Office does not consider this will
                    constitute technical rupture of diplomatic relations and holds that the latter
                    will arise only when and if Paraguay withdraws its Minister from Santiago and
                    places its interests in the hands of a third power.</p>
                <p>Neither the Chilean press nor public is fully aware of the situation as yet and
                    the reaction is consequently mild.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sevier</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
